1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:08,070
DexPilot’s 2019 system lets a visible human hand steer a robot with twenty-three actuated joints.
2019 年的 DexPilot 研究：如何仅靠观察人手，操控具有 23 个驱动关节的机器人。

2
00:00:08,390 --> 00:00:12,050
First, perception estimates where the hand is and how its fingers bend.
首先，感知模块估计手的位置、朝向，以及手指如何弯曲。

3
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:18,470
Then retargeting translates that human configuration into targets the differently shaped robot hand can realize.
接着，重定向把人的手型转成结构不同的机器人手能够实现的目标。

4
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:24,010
Finally, motion generation and torque controllers move the physical robot toward those targets.
最后，运动生成与力矩控制器驱动真实机器人接近这些目标。

5
00:00:24,390 --> 00:00:29,890
Keeping these stages separate explains why accurate tracking alone does not guarantee a successful grasp.
分清这三个环节，才能理解为什么跟踪准确，也未必能成功抓住物体。

6
00:00:30,495 --> 00:00:37,575
The studio uses four calibrated, synchronized RealSense D415 cameras around a black-covered table.
工作区在铺有黑布的桌面周围布置四台经过标定、时间同步的 RealSense D415 相机。

7
00:00:38,055 --> 00:00:42,015
Each depth image supplies surface samples in its own camera coordinates.
每张深度图提供的，都是该相机坐标系中的表面采样。

8
00:00:42,615 --> 00:00:48,755
Back projection and the calibrated camera transformations place those samples into one shared three-dimensional frame.
通过反投影和标定得到的相机变换，这些采样点进入同一个三维坐标系。

9
00:00:49,435 --> 00:00:54,500
Multiple viewpoints improve coverage, but still observe only surfaces visible to the cameras.
多个视角改善了覆盖范围，但得到的仍然只是相机可见的表面。

10
00:00:54,515 --> 00:01:02,275
The reported workspace measures eighty by fifty-five by thirty-eight centimeters, with depth observations ideally within one meter.
论文工作空间为 80 × 55 × 38 厘米，并建议深度观测距离控制在一米以内。

11
00:01:02,862 --> 00:01:09,422
A point cloud contains observed locations, without any definition of fingers, bones, or joints.
点云是一组观测到的位置，本身并不包含手指、骨骼或关节的结构定义。

12
00:01:10,102 --> 00:01:15,702
DexPilot supplies that structure through an articulated hand model assembled from separate surface meshes.
DexPilot 用多个独立表面网格组成带关节的手模型，补上这些结构。

13
00:01:16,182 --> 00:01:21,062
Its twenty revolute joints comprise one spreading joint and three bending joints per finger.
模型共有 20 个转动关节，每根手指包含一个侧向展开关节和三个弯曲关节。

14
00:01:21,682 --> 00:01:28,027
Separately, the whole hand has a rigid position and orientation, often described as its wrist or palm pose.
与手指关节分开，整只手还有刚体位置和朝向，通常称为手腕或手掌位姿。

15
00:01:28,042 --> 00:01:34,682
Moving that global pose carries every finger together; changing finger angles changes the internal configuration.
改变整体位姿会一起移动所有手指；改变手指角度，则会改变手的内部构型。

16
00:01:35,431 --> 00:01:40,991
DART tracks the hand by adjusting this articulated model to match the incoming point cloud.
DART 通过调整这个带关节的模型，使其与输入点云相匹配，从而跟踪人手。

17
00:01:41,431 --> 00:01:46,171
The previous frame usually supplies the starting estimate for its nonlinear optimization.
非线性优化通常以上一帧的估计作为初值。

18
00:01:46,831 --> 00:01:51,531
When that estimate is poor, a plausible but incorrect alignment can trap the optimizer.
一旦初值偏差太大，优化器就可能困在看似合理、实际错误的对齐结果中。

19
00:01:51,931 --> 00:01:57,551
The authors observed severe tracking failures every few minutes without the additional support described next.
作者报告，在后续辅助机制加入前，跟踪可能每隔几分钟就发生严重失败。

20
00:01:57,651 --> 00:02:03,311
Learned pose priors and hand segmentation help steer fitting toward the hand and away from misleading alternatives.
学习得到的位姿先验与手部分割，帮助拟合靠近真正的手，并避开有干扰的解。

21
00:02:03,949 --> 00:02:11,429
This creates a practical problem: training a reliable predictor first requires reliable examples of hand motion.
这带来一个实际问题：训练可靠的预测网络，首先需要可靠的人手运动样本。

22
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:17,009
DexPilot bootstraps those examples with a colored glove used during offline data collection.
DexPilot 在离线采集阶段使用彩色手套，启动这套标注流程。

23
00:02:17,369 --> 00:02:22,029
Visible color patches help estimate the global hand pose and isolate the hand points.
可见的色块帮助估计整手位姿，并从场景中分离出手部点。

24
00:02:22,409 --> 00:02:27,894
DART then fits the depth observations and supplies pose, joint, and segmentation annotations for training.
随后，DART 拟合深度观测，提供训练所需的位姿、关节和分割标注。

25
00:02:27,909 --> 00:02:34,029
These are tracker-generated labels, so calling them ground truth does not make them independent physical measurements.
这些是跟踪器生成的标签，因此即使论文称其为真值，也不等于独立的物理测量。

26
00:02:34,702 --> 00:02:40,302
The glove carries five fingertip patches and three distinct patches on the back of the palm.
手套在五个指尖各有一个色块，手背另有三个颜色不同的色块。

27
00:02:41,182 --> 00:02:46,682
Color thresholding produces patch masks, whose centers become two-dimensional training labels.
颜色阈值分割生成色块掩膜，再用其中心位置形成二维训练标签。

28
00:02:47,062 --> 00:02:53,322
Because lighting changes those thresholds, the authors collect fifty thousand images across different days.
光照变化会影响阈值，因此作者跨多天采集了五万张图像。

29
00:02:54,042 --> 00:03:00,187
GloveNet uses an anti-aliased ResNet backbone and spatial softmax to predict eight keypoint locations.
GloveNet 采用抗混叠的 ResNet 主干与空间 softmax，预测八个关键点的位置。

30
00:03:00,202 --> 00:03:07,422
Background replacement and image augmentation discourage the network from confusing unrelated colors with glove markers.
背景替换和图像增强减少网络把无关颜色误认为手套标记的情况。

31
00:03:08,152 --> 00:03:13,172
Four shifted versions of each camera image test whether predictions remain consistent.
推理时，每个相机图像生成四个平移版本，检查预测是否一致。

32
00:03:13,512 --> 00:03:19,612
Undoing those shifts reveals prediction variation, which supplies a confidence measure across sixteen images.
撤销这些平移后，十六张图像的预测波动提供置信度依据。

33
00:03:20,092 --> 00:03:26,812
The pipeline rejects unreliable estimates and uses temporal filtering to stabilize the recovered three-dimensional points.
流程会剔除不可靠的估计，并用时间滤波稳定恢复出的三维点。

34
00:03:27,232 --> 00:03:33,597
Nevertheless, fingertip patches change their visible shape under occlusion, making their annotated centers inconsistent.
但在遮挡下，指尖色块的可见形状会变化，导致标注中心不稳定。

35
00:03:33,612 --> 00:03:39,492
The final glove-based pose estimate therefore uses only the three more stable patches on the palm.
因此，最终基于手套的位姿估计只使用手背上三个更稳定的色块。

36
00:03:40,040 --> 00:03:45,120
Depth lifts each predicted palm marker from its image coordinates into three dimensions.
深度信息把每个预测出的手背标记，从图像坐标提升到三维空间。

37
00:03:45,700 --> 00:03:52,400
Camera transformations bring observations into a shared frame, where three markers constrain hand position and orientation.
相机变换再将观测带入共同坐标系，由三个标记约束手的位置与朝向。

38
00:03:52,780 --> 00:04:00,140
A triangle with coordinate axes illustrates this geometry, although the paper does not specify the exact rigid-fitting solver.
可以用带坐标轴的三角形说明这个几何关系，但论文没有说明具体的刚体拟合求解器。

39
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:05,280
The pose also defines a heuristic hand volume, so points outside it can be removed.
该位姿还用于确定一个经验设定的手部包围体，从而移除体积外的点。

40
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:09,880
DART consequently fits the hand instead of sliding its model onto the neighboring forearm.
这样，DART 就能拟合手部，减少模型滑向邻近前臂的情况。

41
00:04:10,406 --> 00:04:15,966
The deployed system removes the glove and works on depth-derived point clouds of the bare hand.
部署后的系统移除手套，处理由深度数据得到的裸手点云。

42
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:21,646
After fitting a plane to remove the table, the remaining cloud still includes the arm and body.
拟合平面并去除桌面后，剩下的点云仍然包含手臂和身体。

43
00:04:22,226 --> 00:04:28,506
Stage one uniformly samples eight thousand one hundred and ninety-two points for a PointNet++ based network.
第一级均匀采样 8192 个点，输入基于 PointNet++ 的网络。

44
00:04:28,886 --> 00:04:34,126
It predicts a hand mask and twenty-three keypoints: twenty on the fingers and three on the palm.
网络预测手部掩膜与 23 个关键点：20 个位于手指，3 个位于手背。

45
00:04:34,586 --> 00:04:41,346
Those twenty-three keypoints describe human geometry; they are distinct from the robot system’s twenty-three actuated joints.
这 23 个关键点描述人手几何，与机器人系统的 23 个驱动关节是不同的概念。

46
00:04:41,814 --> 00:04:46,194
The network does more than compress the scene into a single pose vector.
这个网络并不只是把场景压缩成一个位姿向量。

47
00:04:46,514 --> 00:04:52,534
Each input point predicts offsets toward the keypoints, effectively proposing where those landmarks should lie.
每个输入点预测指向各关键点的偏移，相当于提出这些关节应在何处。

48
00:04:53,194 --> 00:04:59,134
Learned neighborhood masks and hand probabilities weight those proposals before averaging them into keypoint positions.
学习得到的邻域掩膜与手部概率，为这些候选位置加权，再求平均得到关键点。

49
00:04:59,734 --> 00:05:05,999
Euclidean losses train both the offsets and final coordinates, while a classification loss trains hand segmentation.
欧氏损失训练偏移与最终坐标，分类损失则训练手部分割。

50
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:11,594
This lets useful local hand evidence contribute more strongly than irrelevant scene points.
这样，有用的局部手部信息就能比无关的场景点发挥更大作用。

51
00:05:12,335 --> 00:05:17,315
Uniform sampling over the whole scene leaves too few samples on the thin fingers.
对整个场景均匀采样，会使细小的手指只分到很少的点。

52
00:05:17,855 --> 00:05:23,915
Stage two therefore returns to the original cloud and resamples the hand using stage one’s pose and segmentation.
因此，第二级利用第一级的位姿和分割，返回原始点云重新采样手部。

53
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:28,235
With its input focused on the hand, it refines the same twenty-three keypoints.
输入集中在手部后，它进一步修正同一组 23 个关键点。

54
00:05:28,615 --> 00:05:33,475
This stage keeps the keypoint and voting losses but no longer needs the hand-segmentation loss.
这一级保留关键点损失和投票损失，不再需要手部分割损失。

55
00:05:33,935 --> 00:05:39,255
Randomizing the input hand pose during training helps it tolerate imperfect estimates from the first stage.
训练时随机扰动输入手位姿，帮助第二级容忍第一级估计中的误差。

56
00:05:39,821 --> 00:05:48,041
DART’s articulated model needs joint angles, whereas the point networks naturally predict three-dimensional keypoint coordinates.
DART 的关节模型需要关节角，而点云网络自然输出三维关键点坐标。

57
00:05:48,761 --> 00:05:54,721
JointNet bridges these representations by flattening twenty-three points into a vector of sixty-nine numbers.
JointNet 将 23 个点展平为 69 维向量，连接这两种表示。

58
00:05:55,221 --> 00:06:01,201
The appendix specifies two hidden layers followed by an output layer that predicts twenty human finger angles.
附录给出了两个隐藏层与一个输出层，预测人手的 20 个手指关节角。

59
00:06:01,661 --> 00:06:06,626
These estimates become priors for DART, which continues fitting the observed surface geometry.
这些估计成为 DART 的先验，而 DART 继续拟合观测到的表面几何。

60
00:06:06,641 --> 00:06:13,781
The learned prediction provides a useful starting point, and model fitting supplies the subsequent geometric refinement.
学习得到的预测提供有用初值，模型拟合再进行几何细化。

61
00:06:14,414 --> 00:06:20,994
The two point-network stages use one hundred thousand point clouds, collected over seven to eight hours.
两级点云网络使用十万帧点云训练，数据采集耗时七到八小时。

62
00:06:21,474 --> 00:06:27,394
Training takes fifteen hours on one Titan Xp, using multiple hands recorded inside the studio.
在一张 Titan Xp 上训练耗时十五小时，样本来自工作区内的多只人手。

63
00:06:27,814 --> 00:06:36,274
A validation set of seven thousand examples yields reported errors of 9.7 millimeters for keypoints and 1.33 degrees per joint.
在七千个验证样本上，论文报告关键点误差为 9.7 毫米，平均每关节角误差为 1.33 度。

64
00:06:36,654 --> 00:06:43,279
These measurements assess agreement with the available annotations, whose provenance remains the glove-assisted tracking pipeline.
这些数字衡量的是与现有标注的一致程度，而标注来源仍是手套辅助的跟踪流程。

65
00:06:43,294 --> 00:06:50,014
They do not establish the same accuracy for unseen hand shapes, different cameras, or unconstrained environments.
它们并不能证明系统对未见过的手型、不同相机或不受约束的环境也具有相同精度。

66
00:06:50,701 --> 00:06:58,381
The resulting tracker combines learned initialization with an articulated model, rather than relying on either component alone.
最终的跟踪器把学习得到的初值与带关节的模型结合起来，两者共同工作。

67
00:06:58,981 --> 00:07:07,341
Its demonstrated operating conditions include calibrated cameras, a bounded workspace, and hands reasonably close to the model’s geometry.
其展示过的运行条件包括已标定相机、有限工作区，以及几何形状与模型较接近的人手。

68
00:07:07,941 --> 00:07:15,441
The authors identify hand-shape variation, fingertip-contact accuracy, and system latency as remaining limitations.
作者指出，手型差异、指尖接触识别精度，以及系统延迟仍然是限制。

69
00:07:15,661 --> 00:07:21,721
Even a correct human estimate still leaves a different problem: the robot has different fingers and joint axes.
即使人手估计正确，另一个问题仍然存在：机器人具有不同的手指结构与关节轴。

70
00:07:22,121 --> 00:07:29,781
Part two follows that transition, showing how geometric retargeting turns human fingertip relationships into feasible robot grasps.
第二部分将沿着这一步继续，解释几何重定向如何把人手指尖关系转成可实现的机器人抓握。
